infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title One NULL in the subquery: IN survives it, NOT IN collapses
  desc Same NULL, opposite outcomes — a disjunction shrugs it off, a conjunction is poisoned (three-valued logic)
  compares
    - label IN — disjunction (safe)
      children
        - label Expands to x = a OR x = b OR x = NULL
          desc An OR over every list value
        - label The NULL term is UNKNOWN
          desc x = NULL is never true
        - label One true term wins
          desc OR succeeds the moment any real value matches
        - label A genuine match still surfaces
          desc Plain IN is safe; the NULL is harmless
    - label NOT IN — conjunction (trap)
      children
        - label Expands to x <> a AND x <> b AND x <> NULL
          desc An AND over every list value
        - label x <> NULL is UNKNOWN
          desc Never true under three-valued logic
        - label One UNKNOWN poisons the AND
          desc true AND UNKNOWN = UNKNOWN, never true
        - label Every row dropped → 0 rows, no error
          desc WHERE discards UNKNOWN; result silently empty
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
